@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/proposal#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# Draft delivery lineage exported by the Proposal Workbench (BRSF software-development profile). Refine, then validate with the BRSF validator.

ex:Mission a backlog:Mission ; rdfs:label "CareConsent: Patient-Controlled Health Data and Auditable Sharing"@en ; backlog:hasMissionStatement "CareConsent will give Patients a practical way to manage selected health records and decide who may access them, for which purpose and for how long. Clinicians will use consistent, permission-filtered queries to review medication, allergy and observation histories. Encrypted off-chain storage will protect record contents, while smart contracts will register consent changes and commitments to release receipts. A separate research-sharing flow will demonstrate patient approval and compensation using test credits. The semester prototype will use synthetic data and make its trust assumptions and access limits explicit." ; backlog:hasMissionOutcome "A patient will be able to share selected record versions with a named clinician until a chosen expiry time, withdraw future access and check recorded gateway releases. An authorised clinician will obtain a reproducible medication-history answer with supporting records. A separately approved research export will produce a traceable test-credit payment." ; backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived .
ex:Lineage a backlog:Lineage ; backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission ; backlog:adoptsObligationSet backlog:OS_SDLC_v2 .
ex:EndUser1 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Patients"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: Adults managing a chronic condition who need to share medication, allergy and symptom histories with more than one care provider; represented by synthetic profiles in the prototype. - Review their records, choose which versions to share, approve a named recipient for a limited period, revoke access and inspect the release history. (weekly, Responsive web application on a smartphone or laptop with a development wallet.)"@en .
ex:EndUser2 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Clinicians"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: Doctors reviewing the longitudinal history of a patient who has explicitly granted them access; represented by separate clinician accounts during testing. - Request access, inspect permitted records and answer bounded questions about medication use, allergies and recorded observations. (daily, Laptop or desktop browser through the authenticated clinical workspace.)"@en .
ex:EndUser3 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Researchers"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: Research staff requesting a specific dataset for a stated study purpose, with each patient's separate approval; represented by test accounts in the demonstration. - State the research purpose and requested fields, submit an access request, obtain an approved export and inspect the corresponding test-credit receipt. (occasional, Desktop browser through the research request screen.)"@en .
ex:Scope a backlog:ScopeStatement ; backlog:scopeForMission ex:Mission ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:coversArea ex:A1, ex:A2, ex:A3, ex:A4, ex:A5 ; backlog:requiresDeliverable ex:D1, ex:D2, ex:D3, ex:D4, ex:D5, ex:D6, ex:D7 ; backlog:hasScopeExclusion ex:X1, ex:X2, ex:X3, ex:X4, ex:X5, ex:X6, ex:X7 .
ex:A1 a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Health data and semantic model"@en ; backlog:areaLocation "FHIR import service, RDF mapping, terminology catalogue and validation rules." ; backlog:areaMeasure "No implementation yet; planned evaluation uses 50 synthetic patients and 1,000 clinical resources spanning 24 months." .
ex:A2 a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Encrypted storage and integrity"@en ; backlog:areaLocation "Private IPFS nodes, off-chain key service and record-version registry contract." ; backlog:areaMeasure "No stored prototype records yet; one encrypted object and one integrity commitment per accepted resource version." .
ex:A3 a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Consent and access enforcement"@en ; backlog:areaLocation "Consent smart contract, authenticated access gateway and role-specific browser screens." ; backlog:areaMeasure "No implemented grants yet; three user roles, two declared purposes and a planned matrix of at least 20 access-control cases." .
ex:A4 a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Clinical queries and patient audit"@en ; backlog:areaLocation "Temporary Jena datasets, predefined SPARQL templates and patient access-history dashboard." ; backlog:areaMeasure "No query or audit results yet; five query templates, ten labelled query fixtures and release-to-event reconciliation are planned." .
ex:A5 a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Research sharing and evaluation"@en ; backlog:areaLocation "Research request screen, test-credit contract, integration checks and reproducible demonstration package." ; backlog:areaMeasure "No research exports or payments yet; one-patient exports and at least ten settlement cases are planned." .
ex:D1 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Synthetic FHIR R4 dataset, documented RDF mapping, small project ontology, terminology catalogue and SHACL shapes with valid and invalid fixtures."@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:D2 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "AES-256-GCM storage adapter, private IPFS deployment and Solidity registry linking opaque record-version identifiers to ciphertext digests."@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:D3 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Storage checks demonstrating authenticated decryption, tamper rejection and absence of plaintext health fields in blockchain transactions and application logs."@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_NonFunctional .
ex:D4 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Patient-controlled consent contract and access gateway supporting selected versions, named recipients, purpose, expiry and revocation."@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A3 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:D5 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Five SPARQL query templates, clinician results with record provenance, and a patient dashboard reconciling gateway release receipts with blockchain commitments."@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A4 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:D6 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Separately approved research export with a fixed test-credit fee, patient credit balance and duplicate-settlement protection."@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A5 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:D7 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Versioned source, deployment instructions, automated acceptance checks, proposed stakeholder evaluation script and a final demonstration using synthetic data."@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A5 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:X1 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Live hospital, e-Nabız, insurer and wearable integrations."@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "External credentials, institutional agreements and production interfaces are not available; documented FHIR fixtures provide a controlled input boundary." .
ex:X2 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Real patient records, clinical trials and deployment for medical decisions."@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "The semester deliverable is a technical prototype using synthetic data; clinical safety and institutional approval are outside the work plan." .
ex:X3 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Diagnosis, treatment recommendations and automatic allergy or drug-interaction advice."@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "The system retrieves recorded information and does not establish clinical truth or prescribe care." .
ex:X4 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Public-chain production deployment, real-money payments and a commercial health-data marketplace."@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "The research compensation mechanism will be evaluated with valueless credits on a local development chain." .
ex:X5 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Guaranteed deletion of every IPFS copy or revocation of data already downloaded."@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "The gateway can stop future authorised releases, but cannot erase copies retained by recipients or unrelated storage nodes." .
ex:X6 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "General natural-language question answering and unrestricted public SPARQL endpoints."@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Five reviewed query templates provide a testable scope and reduce disclosure and query-injection risks." .
ex:X7 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Separate athlete application, production wallet recovery and a complete SNOMED CT distribution."@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "The first release focuses on chronic-care sharing. Terminology use will be limited to an authorised subset if access is available, with an explicitly labelled local demo catalogue otherwise." .
ex:G1 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Represent the selected chronic-care records consistently and reject malformed imports."@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "Clinical queries need explicit coding, usable dates and reliable links before sharing can be assessed." .
ex:G2 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Store encrypted record versions and detect changes before any decrypted content is returned."@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "A blockchain digest is useful only when the actual returned object is checked against it." .
ex:G3 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Give patients effective control over future gateway access by recipient, purpose, selected versions and time."@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Mission ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A3 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "A consent screen must correspond to an enforced access decision, including refusal paths." .
ex:G4 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Provide reproducible clinical-history answers and patient-visible evidence of gateway releases."@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Mission ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A4 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "The patient and clinician need useful records and an understandable history of the system's sharing actions." .
ex:G5 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Demonstrate a separately consented research export with one traceable patient test-credit payment."@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A5 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "The proposed patient compensation model needs an observable, bounded workflow before commercial assumptions are considered." .
ex:G6 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Keep the implementation and evaluation inside the synthetic-data, local-network and predefined-query boundaries."@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Containment ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A5 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "The semester should deliver the agreed sharing workflow without expanding into hospital integration, clinical decision support or a marketplace." .
ex:Spec a backlog:Specification ; backlog:hasSpecificationText "The prototype shall support Patients, Clinicians and Researchers as separate authenticated roles. A patient may import synthetic FHIR R4 records, view validation errors and register an accepted encrypted version. Each new version shall receive a fresh encryption key and nonce; its digest shall cover the exact encrypted envelope bytes, avoiding dependence on RDF serialisation order. A patient shall approve a recipient, declared purpose, explicit record-version list and expiry. The contract shall bind that immutable list through a scope commitment, and the gateway shall verify the list against it. Requests shall be denied if the grant is absent, revoked, expired, for another recipient or purpose, or excludes any requested version. The server shall use a short-lived wallet-signature challenge bound to the session and chain. An authorised query shall decrypt only permitted objects into a temporary graph, run a reviewed template and return only its permitted projection. Consent shall be checked again immediately before release. A release receipt commitment shall be confirmed on chain before the response is sent; the receipt describes an authorised release attempt rather than proof that a human read it. If the chain, storage, integrity check or audit anchoring is unavailable, release shall fail closed. A research export shall require its own grant and funded test-credit request. Settlement shall be idempotent and shall rely on the explicitly trusted gateway's release attestation. No private key, clinical text, raw CID or plaintext patient identifier shall be placed on chain. The gateway and key service remain trusted components capable of processing plaintext; this is not a claim of trustless or end-to-end private computation." .
ex:Scen1 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Nominal ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a patient has granted a clinician access to selected medication records for treatment until tomorrow, when that clinician runs the antibiotics template within the permitted interval, then only matching permitted records are returned with source versions and a confirmed release receipt commitment." .
ex:Scen2 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given the patient has revoked a clinician's grant, when the clinician repeats a previously successful request, then the gateway refuses it before decryption or result release and exposes no clinical fields." .
ex:Scen3 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Boundary ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a grant expires at time T according to the latest confirmed local-chain block, when access is evaluated at T minus one second it may pass, and when evaluated at T it must fail; authorisation requires current time strictly less than expiry." .
ex:Scen4 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a researcher holds a treatment-only grant or asks for an unselected allergy record, when an export is requested, then the purpose or scope mismatch is rejected and no credit settlement occurs." .
ex:Scen5 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given an encrypted object differs from its anchored digest or fails authenticated decryption, when a permitted recipient requests it, then the object is rejected without returning any partial plaintext." .
ex:Scen6 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Absent ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a valid grant covers a patient with no antibiotic records in the requested interval, when the template runs, then the workspace displays an explicit no-matching-records result, distinct from denied access or missing storage." .
ex:Scen7 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given the chain cannot confirm a release receipt, when an otherwise authorised response is prepared, then the gateway returns a service-unavailable result without releasing clinical content or settling research credits." .
ex:O1 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Validate and map the planned synthetic evaluation dataset."@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G1 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "A reproducible validation run counts accepted resources, linked patient profiles, mapped resource types and rejected negative fixtures. Expected resource identifiers are compared before and after mapping." ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0 imported or mapped prototype records; no validation run has been performed." ; backlog:hasTargetValue "50 synthetic patient profiles and 1,000 valid clinical resources mapped; all 20 deliberately malformed fixtures rejected with a specific reason." ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O2 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Verify every accepted encrypted version and reject tampered objects."@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G2 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Derived ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "For all 1,000 resource versions, compare SHA-256 of the retrieved encrypted envelope with its registry commitment and attempt authenticated decryption. Repeat with 20 mutated objects and incorrect keys." ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0 verified prototype versions; integrity and encryption checks are not implemented." ; backlog:hasTargetValue "1,000 successful round trips for valid versions, 20 of 20 tampered or wrong-key cases rejected, and no plaintext clinical fields found in the inspected chain and application logs." ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O3 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Enforce the complete consent decision matrix."@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G3 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Derived ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Execute at least 20 cases spanning valid grants, wrong recipient, wrong purpose, missing grant, excluded version, expiry boundary, revocation, replay and concurrent revoke-before-release. Inspect responses and key-service calls." ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0 implemented or executed access-control cases." ; backlog:hasTargetValue "100% of specified denial cases return no clinical result or decryption key, and every specified valid case succeeds when dependencies are available." ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O4 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Return correct permission-filtered answers and reconcile release receipts."@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G4 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Derived ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Compare five templates over ten manually labelled synthetic query fixtures with expected record identifiers; join all successful gateway release attempts to event commitments. Measure 100 authorised local requests, excluding initial import, on a documented machine." ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0 verified query fixtures or reconciled release receipts; response latency is not yet measured." ; backlog:hasTargetValue "10 of 10 fixtures match exactly, no cross-patient or out-of-scope result appears, 100% of successful release attempts have a matching event commitment, and local p95 response time is at most 3 seconds." ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O5 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Settle approved research sharing once per release identifier."@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G5 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Derived ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Execute ten settlement cases covering a funded approved export, refusal, expiry, insufficient funds, an untrusted attester and duplicate retries. Compare the patient's credit balance with settlement events." ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0 approved exports and 0 settlement cases implemented or executed." ; backlog:hasTargetValue "All ten cases match their expected outcomes; an approved export credits its stated fee exactly once, while denied and unfunded requests transfer nothing." ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O6 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Deliver a reproducible prototype without crossing the agreed scope boundaries."@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G6 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Review every merged feature against A1-A5 and E1-E6; inspect fixtures, configuration and the demonstration script for real records, public deployment, real-money transfers and unplanned integrations." ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0 implementation artefacts reviewed; the project is at proposal stage." ; backlog:hasTargetValue "Every merged feature traces to a planned epic, all acceptance fixtures are synthetic, and zero excluded integrations or real-money features are required by the release." ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Hold .
ex:Model_Activity a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ActivityDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "Start -> authenticate the account with a fresh wallet challenge -> choose import, access request or patient review. Import branch: validate FHIR and project shapes; on failure show field-level errors and stop; on success encrypt a new version, pin ciphertext, confirm the digest registration and show it in the manifest. Sharing branch: a recipient submits scope, purpose and duration; the patient refuses or signs a grant. Access branch: check confirmed grant state and scope; on failure return denial; on success fetch and verify ciphertext, decrypt into a temporary dataset and run the selected query or export projection. Recheck consent immediately before release; if it changed, discard the prepared response. Otherwise confirm a receipt commitment and send the result. For a funded research export, record one settlement using the release identifier. Close the temporary dataset after either success or failure. Expiry and revocation block later releases, while earlier receipts remain visible." .
ex:Model_Sequence a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_SequenceDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "Patient browser -> gateway: signed challenge and synthetic FHIR import. Gateway -> validator: resource and shape checks. Gateway -> key service: generate and wrap a per-version key. Gateway -> private IPFS: encrypted envelope; IPFS -> gateway: CID. Patient browser -> registry contract: sign registration of an opaque version identifier and ciphertext digest. Clinician browser -> gateway: request named versions for treatment. Patient browser -> consent contract: sign the recipient, scope commitment, purpose and expiry. Clinician browser -> gateway: run a query template with a grant identifier. Gateway -> contract: read current confirmed grant. Gateway -> IPFS and key service: fetch verified ciphertext and unwrap authorised keys. Gateway -> embedded Jena: build the scoped temporary dataset and execute the bound template. Gateway -> contract: recheck permission and anchor a release receipt commitment. After confirmation, gateway -> clinician: projected result and receipt reference. Gateway closes the dataset. The research variant adds an approved funded request and an idempotent gateway-attested settlement transaction." .
ex:Model_Class a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ClassDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "PatientProfile(patientId, ownerAccount) owns 0..* HealthRecordVersion(versionId, resourceType, recordedAt, status, ciphertextDigest, replacesVersion). A version belongs to exactly one patient. Its protected StorageManifest entry holds CID, wrappedKeyRef and the RDF mapping version; these fields are not public contract data. TerminologyConcept(system, code, label, catalogueVersion) codes record properties. AccessRequest(requestId, requester, purpose, requestedVersionList, requestedUntil, fee) may produce one ConsentGrant(grantId, owner, grantee, purposeCode, scopeCommitment, expiresAt, revoked). The immutable encrypted scope manifest resolves the commitment to versions. ReleaseReceipt(releaseId, grantId, requester, versions, releasedAt, outcome, eventTx) describes a gateway release attempt. PROV-O links a query or export activity to its source versions and output. ResearchSettlement(releaseId, fee, patientAccount, settled) references one approved research release. Superseded records remain historically identifiable; retiring a record removes it from new selection without rewriting its earlier chain commitment." .
ex:Backlog a backlog:Backlog ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:appliesDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD .
ex:DoD a backlog:DefinitionOfDone ; backlog:hasDoDCriterion ex:DoD1, ex:DoD2, ex:DoD3, ex:DoD4, ex:DoD5, ex:DoD6 .
ex:DoD1 a backlog:DoDCriterion ; rdfs:label "The story meets its specified nominal and refusal outcomes."@en ; backlog:hasCheckQuery "Run its linked acceptance cases against a clean synthetic fixture set; attach actual results and evidence at final submission." .
ex:DoD2 a backlog:DoDCriterion ; rdfs:label "Authorisation is enforced at the gateway and contract boundary."@en ; backlog:hasCheckQuery "Review recipient, purpose, version list, time and revocation checks; denial cases must expose no health result or key." .
ex:DoD3 a backlog:DoDCriterion ; rdfs:label "Stored and returned versions are traceable and verifiable."@en ; backlog:hasCheckQuery "Check encrypted-envelope digest verification and the link from result to source version and confirmed receipt event." .
ex:DoD4 a backlog:DoDCriterion ; rdfs:label "Sensitive content stays out of public interfaces and routine logs."@en ; backlog:hasCheckQuery "Inspect transaction calldata, events, browser responses, application logs and storage objects using planted synthetic identifiers and clinical strings." .
ex:DoD5 a backlog:DoDCriterion ; rdfs:label "The work is reproducible and within scope."@en ; backlog:hasCheckQuery "A second team member can follow the setup instructions, replay the synthetic demonstration and identify the epic and module for the change." .
ex:DoD6 a backlog:DoDCriterion ; rdfs:label "The feature has a named owner, peer review and usable screens."@en ; backlog:hasCheckQuery "Before implementation is accepted, assign actual team members, review the change and walk through success, empty, denied and unavailable states." .
ex:Initiative a backlog:Initiative ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:hasInitiativeKind backlog:Kind_InitialDevelopment ; backlog:decomposesInto ex:E1, ex:E2, ex:E3, ex:E4, ex:E5, ex:E6 .
ex:E1 a backlog:Epic ; rdfs:label "Import and model chronic-care records"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:O1 ; backlog:decomposesInto ex:S1 .
ex:E2 a backlog:Epic ; rdfs:label "Protect and verify stored record versions"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:O2 ; backlog:decomposesInto ex:S2, ex:S11 .
ex:E3 a backlog:Epic ; rdfs:label "Enforce patient-controlled sharing permissions"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:O3 ; backlog:decomposesInto ex:S3, ex:S4, ex:S5 .
ex:E4 a backlog:Epic ; rdfs:label "Answer bounded clinical-history questions"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:O4 ; backlog:decomposesInto ex:S6, ex:S7 .
ex:E5 a backlog:Epic ; rdfs:label "Explain and verify the patient's sharing history"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:O4 ; backlog:decomposesInto ex:S8, ex:S12 .
ex:E6 a backlog:Epic ; rdfs:label "Demonstrate compensated research sharing within the agreed scope"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:pursuesObjective ex:O5 ; backlog:decomposesInto ex:S9, ex:S10 .
ex:S1 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "import a structured medication, allergy, condition or observation record"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Patients" ; backlog:wantsCapability "import a structured medication, allergy, condition or observation record" ; backlog:soThat "my selected health history can be interpreted consistently" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Data ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC1 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score1 .
ex:AC1 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a supported synthetic FHIR record with a valid patient reference, when I import it, then the system accepts it and creates a traceable RDF representation; an invalid record instead returns a field-specific error without registration." .
ex:Score1 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "5"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S2 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "store an encrypted and verifiable version of each accepted record"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Patients" ; backlog:wantsCapability "store an encrypted and verifiable version of each accepted record" ; backlog:soThat "storage nodes cannot read its clinical contents and later changes can be detected" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Architecture ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC2 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score2 .
ex:AC2 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given an accepted record, when it is stored, then only an authenticated encrypted envelope is pinned and its digest is registered; a changed envelope or wrong key prevents all plaintext release." .
ex:Score2 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "4.1"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S3 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "grant a named clinician access to selected versions until a chosen expiry"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Patients" ; backlog:wantsCapability "grant a named clinician access to selected versions until a chosen expiry" ; backlog:soThat "sharing is limited to the appointment's needs" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Security ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC3 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score3 .
ex:AC3 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a request for selected medication versions, when I sign a treatment grant, then only that recipient, purpose and immutable version list is authorised before expiry; a different recipient or additional version is denied." .
ex:Score3 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "5"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S4 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "revoke an existing grant"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Patients" ; backlog:wantsCapability "revoke an existing grant" ; backlog:soThat "future releases through the application stop" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Security ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC4 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score4 .
ex:AC4 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a currently valid grant, when my revocation transaction is confirmed, then every subsequent release check denies that grant, including a prepared response awaiting its final check; the interface explains that earlier downloaded copies remain outside this control." .
ex:Score4 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "5.8"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S5 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "see whether my requested access is pending, active, refused, expired or revoked"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Clinicians" ; backlog:wantsCapability "see whether my requested access is pending, active, refused, expired or revoked" ; backlog:soThat "I understand whether a patient-authorised review is available" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Interaction ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC5 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score5 .
ex:AC5 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given I have submitted a request, when I open its status, then the application shows the current request and grant state without exposing any health fields before permission is active." .
ex:Score5 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "6.7"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S6 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "list recorded antibiotic use overlapping the previous twelve months"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Clinicians" ; backlog:wantsCapability "list recorded antibiotic use overlapping the previous twelve months" ; backlog:soThat "I can review the permitted medication history before consultation" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Interface ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC6 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score6 .
ex:AC6 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a valid medication grant and a fixed evaluation interval, when I run the antibiotic template, then it returns exactly the permitted matching MedicationStatement versions, excludes entered-in-error records and includes their source dates and versions; a prescription alone is not presented as confirmed use." .
ex:Score6 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "4.8"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S7 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "review active recorded conditions, active allergies and dated symptom or exercise observations"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Clinicians" ; backlog:wantsCapability "review active recorded conditions, active allergies and dated symptom or exercise observations" ; backlog:soThat "I can inspect a coherent permitted history without opening separate reports" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Data ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC7 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score7 .
ex:AC7 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given grants covering the relevant record types, when I run each of the four remaining templates, then the results match the labelled fixtures and contain only permitted patient records; an empty match is distinguished from denial or a missing object." .
ex:Score7 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "4.2"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S8 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "inspect who received records through the gateway and when"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Patients" ; backlog:wantsCapability "inspect who received records through the gateway and when" ; backlog:soThat "I can review the application's sharing actions" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Interface_UI ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC8 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score8 .
ex:AC8 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given an authorised release attempt, when I open its history entry, then I see the recipient, purpose, versions, time and a receipt commitment matching a confirmed chain event; the entry does not claim to prove later human viewing or onward sharing." .
ex:Score8 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "4.8"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S9 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "request a narrow dataset for a stated study purpose and test-credit fee"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Researchers" ; backlog:wantsCapability "request a narrow dataset for a stated study purpose and test-credit fee" ; backlog:soThat "the patient can make a separate informed sharing decision" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Interface_UI ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC9 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score9 .
ex:AC9 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given no research grant exists, when I request an export with selected versions, requested fields, expiry and fee, then the patient sees those terms and can approve or refuse; a treatment grant cannot authorise this export." .
ex:Score9 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "4"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S10 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "receive the agreed test-credit fee once for an approved research release"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Patients" ; backlog:wantsCapability "receive the agreed test-credit fee once for an approved research release" ; backlog:soThat "the proposed compensation flow is transparent and checkable" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Security ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC10 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score10 .
ex:AC10 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given an approved research grant and sufficient funded test credits, when the trusted gateway attests an authorised export release, then the contract credits the stated fee to my development account once and emits a settlement event; repeating the same release identifier cannot pay again." .
ex:Score10 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "3.2"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S11 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "create a corrected version without silently changing earlier records"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Patients" ; backlog:wantsCapability "create a corrected version without silently changing earlier records" ; backlog:soThat "the history remains traceable and old permissions do not silently expand" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Data ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC11 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score11 .
ex:AC11 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a registered version and a grant covering it, when I import a correction, then a new version with a fresh key and digest is created; the earlier commitment remains, and sharing the correction requires explicit inclusion in a new grant." .
ex:Score11 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "5.8"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:S12 a backlog:Story ; rdfs:label "receive a clear failure message when a safe release cannot be completed"@en ; backlog:memberOfContainer ex:Backlog ; backlog:asRole "Patients" ; backlog:wantsCapability "receive a clear failure message when a safe release cannot be completed" ; backlog:soThat "I can distinguish a system problem from an empty medical history" ; backlog:hasInvestmentCategory backlog:Cat_NewCapability ; backlog:hasApplicableConcern backlog:Concern_Interface ; backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion ex:AC12 ; backlog:hasPriorityScore ex:Score12 .
ex:AC12 a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ; backlog:hasGherkinText "Given storage is missing or the chain cannot confirm the receipt, when a recipient asks for my records, then the gateway releases no clinical content, returns a distinct unavailable result and leaves the request eligible for a safe retry." .
ex:Score12 a backlog:PriorityScore ; backlog:scoredByMethod backlog:Method_WSJF ; backlog:hasScoreValue "6"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:TC1 a backlog:TestCase ; backlog:hasCaseText "Accept supported records and reject malformed imports before storage registration." ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:S1 ; backlog:runsOnData ex:TD1 .
ex:TD1 a backlog:TestData ; backlog:hasFixtureState "Valid synthetic Condition, MedicationStatement, AllergyIntolerance and Observation resources; 20 negative fixtures with missing patient links, invalid types, unsupported modifiers or inconsistent dates." .
ex:TC2 a backlog:TestCase ; backlog:hasCaseText "Round-trip valid ciphertext and reject tampering or wrong-key decryption." ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:S2 ; backlog:runsOnData ex:TD2 .
ex:TD2 a backlog:TestData ; backlog:hasFixtureState "1,000 generated clinical resources; 20 altered envelopes or incorrect keys; two encryptions of the same resource to check fresh nonce/key use." .
ex:TC3 a backlog:TestCase ; backlog:hasCaseText "Enforce recipient, purpose, scope and expiry on direct API calls as well as UI requests." ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:S3 ; backlog:runsOnData ex:TD3 .
ex:TD3 a backlog:TestData ; backlog:hasFixtureState "Patient P01, two clinician accounts, one researcher, selected medication versions and an excluded allergy version; evaluate at expiry minus one second and exactly expiry." .
ex:TC4 a backlog:TestCase ; backlog:hasCaseText "Reject new access and a prepared response after confirmed revocation." ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:S4 ; backlog:runsOnData ex:TD4 .
ex:TD4 a backlog:TestData ; backlog:hasFixtureState "One active grant, a confirmed revoke transaction and a controlled pause before the gateway's final permission check; replay the prior request after revocation." .
ex:TC5 a backlog:TestCase ; backlog:hasCaseText "Show each request state without disclosing clinical payloads." ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:S5 ; backlog:runsOnData ex:TD5 .
ex:TD5 a backlog:TestData ; backlog:hasFixtureState "Pending, refused, active, expired and revoked fixtures; inspect both rendered status and network responses." .
ex:TC6 a backlog:TestCase ; backlog:hasCaseText "Return the exact allowed antibiotic record identifiers at temporal boundaries." ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:S6 ; backlog:runsOnData ex:TD6 .
ex:TD6 a backlog:TestData ; backlog:hasFixtureState "Evaluation time 2026-12-01T00:00:00Z and interval [2025-12-01T00:00:00Z, 2026-12-01T00:00:00Z); include overlapping use periods, non-antibiotics, entered-in-error statements, excluded versions and another patient." .
ex:TC7 a backlog:TestCase ; backlog:hasCaseText "Check the four remaining templates against labelled results and handle an empty permitted graph." ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:S7 ; backlog:runsOnData ex:TD7 .
ex:TD7 a backlog:TestData ; backlog:hasFixtureState "Active and inactive conditions and allergies, symptom observations, exercise observations, different units, missing optional fields and a patient with no matching records; ten query fixtures in total across S6-S7." .
ex:TC8 a backlog:TestCase ; backlog:hasCaseText "Reconcile private receipt details with confirmed event commitments and detect receipt modification." ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:S8 ; backlog:runsOnData ex:TD8 .
ex:TD8 a backlog:TestData ; backlog:hasFixtureState "Successful releases for two recipients, one altered receipt and one interrupted response after anchoring; label the latter as an attempted release with delivery unconfirmed." .
ex:TC9 a backlog:TestCase ; backlog:hasCaseText "Require separate research approval and show requested fields, purpose, duration and fee." ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:S9 ; backlog:runsOnData ex:TD9 .
ex:TD9 a backlog:TestData ; backlog:hasFixtureState "A valid treatment grant, no research grant, a pending research request and approved/refused variants; selected direct-identifier fields must be excluded from the research projection." .
ex:TC10 a backlog:TestCase ; backlog:hasCaseText "Pay the approved fee once and reject unfunded, unauthorised and repeated settlements." ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:S10 ; backlog:runsOnData ex:TD10 .
ex:TD10 a backlog:TestData ; backlog:hasFixtureState "Ten settlement fixtures using valueless local credits, including sufficient funds, insufficient funds, wrong attester, expired grant, missing release attestation and duplicate release identifiers." .
ex:TC11 a backlog:TestCase ; backlog:hasCaseText "Keep old commitments intact and require fresh consent for a corrected version." ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:S11 ; backlog:runsOnData ex:TD11 .
ex:TD11 a backlog:TestData ; backlog:hasFixtureState "Two versions of one medication statement with distinct keys, nonces, digests and CIDs; an existing grant names only the first version." .
ex:TC12 a backlog:TestCase ; backlog:hasCaseText "Fail closed on storage, key-service or chain failure and retry safely." ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:S12 ; backlog:runsOnData ex:TD12 .
ex:TD12 a backlog:TestData ; backlog:hasFixtureState "Unavailable IPFS object, failed key unwrap, rejected audit transaction, stale chain connection and a repeated request with the same release identifier." .
